Treat it as a rule and expand it into concrete dates for the week you're showing. With date-fns-tz:

ts
import { zonedTimeToUtc } from 'date-fns-tz';

function slotToUtc(weekStart: Date, day: number, hhmm: string, tz: string) {
  const d = new Date(weekStart);
  d.setDate(d.getDate() + day);
  const [h, m] = hhmm.split(':').map(Number);
  const local = `${d.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}T${String(h).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(m).padStart(2, '0')}:00`;
  return zonedTimeToUtc(local, tz);
}


Then compute overlaps in UTC and convert back to each viewer's zone for display. The offset now comes from the actual date, so it's right on either side of the DST change.

