Nice, clean deletion. Here's a tightened version:

ts
export type Day = 'mon' | 'tue' | 'wed' | 'thu' | 'fri' | 'sat' | 'sun';

export type SlotState = 'available' | 'unavailable' | 'unset';

export interface Slot {
  day: Day;
  hour: number; // 0-23
  state: SlotState;
  userId?: string;
}

export type Grid = Slot[][];

export interface GridProps {
  grid: Grid;
  onChange: (next: Grid) => void;
}


The main change is replacing `boolean | null` with a named `SlotState`, which makes the three cases explicit. Removing `any` and `Function` will surface real type errors, so run `npx tsc --noEmit` after.

Those are the expected fallout. For the null checks, swap them like this:

ts
// before
slot.available === null
// after
slot.state === 'unset'

// before
slot.available === true
// after
slot.state === 'available'


For the API day, narrow it at the boundary instead of casting everywhere:

ts
const DAYS = ['mon','tue','wed','thu','fri','sat','sun'] as const;

export function isDay(v: string): v is Day {
  return (DAYS as readonly string[]).includes(v);
}


Then filter or throw in your API mapper when `isDay` fails. If the API payload still uses the `available` boolean, convert it to `state` in that same mapper so the rest of the app only sees the new shape.
